# Pairing (docs/pageflip.md section 8.1), LEFT half: it walks to the pairing screen, waits for the
# other instance to appear on it, and selects it.
#
# Both instances have to be on this screen at once. That is the design, not a limitation of the
# harness: beacons only go out from here, so a device can only be discovered by somebody who also
# asked to pair.
#
# The route was established with sim_pageflip_pairing_probe.script rather than guessed. Home's menu
# is [continue reading, Browse Files, Recent Books, File Transfer, Settings]; inside Settings row 0
# is the tab bar and Confirm on it cycles Display -> Reader; Up from row 0 wraps to the last entry
# of the tab, which is where the pairing action is appended.
log pageflip-pairing-left: start
expect_timeout 90000
expect Entering activity: Home
wait 1000
tap down
tap down
tap down
tap down
wait 500
tap confirm
expect Entering activity: Settings
wait 1500
tap confirm
wait 800
tap up
wait 800
tap confirm
expect Entering activity: PageFlipPairing
# Beacons go out once a second; four seconds is comfortably past the first exchange.
wait 4000
screenshot /screenshots/pf-pairing-left-00.bmp
# Row 0 is "any nearby device"; the discovered one is the row below it.
tap down
wait 800
screenshot /screenshots/pf-pairing-left-01.bmp
tap confirm
# The notice holds for 2.5s and then the screen closes itself.
wait 1200
screenshot /screenshots/pf-pairing-left-02.bmp
wait 2500
log pageflip-pairing-left: done
quit
